WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.299
Speaker 1: We've been covering the Anti-woke
movement being in shambles.

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:07.770
And we have another data point in this that
I want to show you right now.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:18.570
A new Gallup study finds that same sex marriage
support is at an all time high, 71% in the

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.220
United States.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.660
The highlights here are this figure matches
the highest recorded one in history, which

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.640
was last year.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.930
Support is lowest among Republicans and weekly
churchgoers.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:34.080
If you're a Republican, only a 49% chance
you support gay marriage.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.960
If you go to church weekly, only a 41%.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:43.090
Young adults and Democrats are the groups
most supportive of gay marriage.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:47.750
If you look at the historical chart, this
goes back to 1996.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.469
You see that in 1996 there was 27% support
for gay marriage.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:59.329
And in other words, the belief that same sex
couples should be recognized under the law.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:05.210
Just like opposite sex couples that has climbed
and climbed and climbed all the way up to

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.380
71%, 71%.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:15.310
If you look at different groups, you find
that in terms of church attendance, the more

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:20.220
you go to church, the less likely you are
to support gay marriage.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.119
Women, slightly more than men, support gay
marriage, but the numbers are very, very,

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:26.150
very close.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:32.500
And then basically, from 50 years of age and
up, you're less likely to support gay marriage.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.010
The group most likely to support gay marriage
is those 18 to 29.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:40.259
If you went to college, are more likely to
support gay marriage than if you didn't.

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:44.670
Obviously, Democrats more likely than independents
and Republicans to support it.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.950
Regionally, we see that the South has the
lowest support for gay marriage.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.850
So what does this tell us?

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.520
This tells us tells us a number of different
things.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.780
Number one, it tells us that the so-called
culture war that the right loves to say they're

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:06.869
prevailing in when it comes to so-called boys
and girls sports and woke ideology and drag

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:09.009
and all of these things.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:10.929
The right is losing.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:14.310
You can't find any empirical data that the
right is winning.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.230
You ask about abortion.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:21.670
Support for abortion being legal in most situations
is higher than ever during the Roe v Wade

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:22.670
era.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.670
Today.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.090
Today, support for gay marriage is higher
than ever.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:33.370
You ask people, Do you think we've done enough,
not enough or the right amount when it comes

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:39.470
to making transpeople feel welcome in society?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.760
The majority says we have either done the
right amount or not enough.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.200
That's the and that's not the Anti-woke position.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.000
I hate to break it to these folks.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.870
So that's why the right is trying to steal
